  "id": "clubfoot",
  "term": "clubfoot",
  "definition": "Clubfoot, also called congenital talipes equinovarus, is a common birth-related foot deformity in which the ankle and foot are turned into an abnormal position. It involves ankle equinus, inward turning of the hindfoot, a high arch, and inward bending of the front of the foot, often with calf muscle wasting, and may occur on its own or with other conditions.",
